# Project — FE II album covers (R3F aggregator)

## Stack
- Build: Vite (pins = `react-template`; do not bump without the instructor)
- UI: React 19, plain CSS (`src/index.css`, colours from `src/theme/tokens.js`)
- 3D: three.js + @react-three/fiber + @react-three/drei (when a route chooses WebGL)
- Routing: react-router-dom — one instructor-owned router in `src/App.jsx`
- Language: JavaScript + JSDoc typedefs (`src/lib/types.js`). No TypeScript, no `tsc`
- Assets: per-route PNG sources in `covers/<slug>/public/`; KTX2 (ETC1S or UASTC) via `scripts/encode-cover.mjs` when the route uses textures
- No shadcn/ui, no Tailwind, no cloud LLM SDK dependencies

## Repo structure (enforce)
- `src/` — instructor-owned gallery: router, `/covers/:slug` shell, shared `lib/`. Students do not edit it
- `src/lib/` — shared helpers (BudgetProbe, budget verdict, reduced-motion hook, JSDoc typedefs)
- `covers/registry.json` — one `{ slug, title, authors, concept, thumbnail, tags, readiness }` object per route
- `covers/<slug>/src/Route.jsx` — default export; complete endpoint (DOM, WebGL, or hybrid)
- `covers/<slug>/public/` — pictures + gallery thumbnail; reference with `new URL('../public/<file>', import.meta.url).href`
- `covers/<slug>/docs/` — renderer-info, shader-note, ktx2-note, ai-3d-merge-log (honest N/A when a bar does not apply)
- `covers/_template/` — neutral starters, never a route; `covers/_studio/` — instructor reference only
- `scripts/` — Node pipelines (registry check, toktx encode)

## Route contract (do not break)
- Each slug is a complete endpoint (D26). The shell lazy-loads `Route.jsx` and does not wrap student work in a shared Canvas
- A route never replaces `src/App.jsx`, never edits another slug's folder (except task4 with consent)

## Engineering values
- Prefer explicit modules over barrel files
- JavaScript only — validate shapes with JSDoc typedefs where helpful
- Unmount cleanup: dispose WebGL resources, cancel rAF, remove `document.documentElement` scope classes
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for any motion you add
- Album title and controls stay in the DOM when possible, not burned into the WebGL buffer

## Git hygiene
- Branch `cover-<slug>-task<N>-<short-topic-name>` from `main`; change only your slug + one registry object
- Never commit uncompressed multi-megabyte PNGs as runtime textures; ship the chosen KTX2 when you use KTX2
- No commercial album art without a declared right (photo of an album you own, or a named licence)

## When unsure
- Read `CONTRIBUTING.md` (route contract, PR ritual) and your route's `docs/` before adding effects
